+## Export and validation scope
 
-## Edit a map
+Draw/finish a region, generate a loop, place a charger staging pose and export the
+existing RegionRegistry v1. The owner export uses existing tangent checkpoints;
+the reviewed PATROL asset then uses the existing arc-length checkpoints and
+`path_file` dense-route binding. R8-A4 Mission Manager performs GOTO then admits
+the dense PATROL path through Facade into two finite FollowPath segments; the
+older independent-checkpoint execution note in the legacy validator is not a
+claim about this current runtime chain.
 
-1. Keep **Saved Campus map** selected to use the saved RTAB OccupancyGrid and its checksum-bound Campus Keepout profile. Select another saved map from the menu when one is available. The built-in **DEMO fixture** exists only for a successful example and never represents a surveyed map.
-2. Click **New region**, draw three or more vertices on the map, and click **Complete boundary** (or Enter). Scroll to zoom and drag with the right mouse button to pan. Select a region, drag its boundary vertices to adjust them, or Shift+click a vertex to remove it. After a boundary edit, click Generate again to refresh the preview.
-3. Select a region, choose the safety margin, direction, and patrol preview laps, then click **Generate safe perimeter loop**. The tool reports the specific geometry/turning/mission-budget failure when no candidate passes.
-4. Click **Add charger**, click its staging position, then click an arrow direction. The right panel lets you edit the ID/name/pose, replace the map mark, or delete it. Export checks footprint clearance.
-5. Save the editable project to continue later. **Export Mission Registry** emits the existing v1 schema and a separate offline validation report. The map id, revision, and OccupancyGrid SHA must match when reopening; the editor will reject a different map snapshot.
+[Current result](../../docs/validation/R9_REGULAR_SITE_RESULT.md) records real-map
+sweeps, new entry, Registry and actual SMAC static replay. Geometry/static planning
+PASS is not tracking/full-lap PASS. `motion_validated=false` remains. No startup
+runner, authorization, runtime Gate or dynamic task was added.
 
-The standalone Campus map in this repository is roughly 12.8 × 15.15 m. It has a separate formal Keepout mask and only about 36.67 m² of known free space after that mask. The current vehicle profile has a 1.10 × 0.68 m footprint, 1.12 m minimum turn radius, and the planner reserves a 3% radius margin plus the selected safety distance. The editor never changes map, Keepout, or Mission files.
+## Reproducible fixtures and known history
 
-## Verification limits
+`tests/fixtures/SOURCES.json` records SHA256 of every exact gzip capture from the
+real Pillar map/Keepout, legacy Campus export and projection reference. No RTAB DB
+is bundled; a test-only model uses decoded captured grids/masks. It never claims
+to validate a production map DB or bypasses production MapModel loading. Synthetic
+demo tests remain explicitly labelled separately.
 
-Green means the dense closed curve passed geometry checks against known-free map cells and Keepout, its circumscribed vehicle disk, boundary margin, and turn-radius sampling. It does not mean Smac will follow every leg or that the vehicle has driven it. Mission currently executes each route checkpoint as a separate NavigateToPose goal, so it stops and releases Lease at segment boundaries. A saved Smac path can be checked through local `POST /api/check-planner-path` with JSON fields `boundary`, `candidate_dense`, `actual_poses` (each `[x,y,yaw]`), and optional `corridor` in metres. The result checks obstacle sweep, region boundary, route corridor, and sampled curvature. Actual tracking still needs a separately authorized Gazebo run.
+The10 historical setup errors came from eager loading the old Campus default:
+52550 unknown cells used gray205, interpreted as free at free_thresh=.25;24677
+free cells used254 instead of the validator's255, yielding77227 exact-image
+mismatches. Tests now isolate inputs, reproduce that failure from exact captured
+bytes, and exercise the real current site without mutating historical assets.
+Original failure logs/SHAs remain in the validation archive. Geometry assertions
+were retained; only fixture binding/provenance classification changed.
 
-The exported demo file deliberately has `DEMO-perimeter-15m` identity. Mission's loader accepts its structure, but its map hash cannot match the real Campus map. Do not treat the demo configuration as a real location registry.
